{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mummy-the-curse/68689-is-mummy-destined-to-have-a-big-battle-at-the-kickoff","id":68689,"title":"Is mummy destined to have a big battle at the kickoff?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Mummy: The Curse"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-09T16:14:35-08:00","id":68689,"title":"Is mummy destined to have a big battle at the kickoff?","content":"This is related to my other thread about how mummy lends itself to being a one chronicle game.<br /> <br /> Is mummy designed to have a big battle at the beginning of the chronicle, similar to how movies like Gladiator, Saving private Ryan, and Enemy at the Gates started the movies with a big battle to get the audience right into the action. The reason being, quite simply, is that the beginning is when the mummies are at the top of their game and brimming with power. However, the nature of the descent means that they pretty have only a day or two to really enjoy the really awesome power, so why not have fun and put it to use in a big fight at the start. <br /> <br /> More specifically, the opening scene would pretty much have to be a mook bash against the minions of the bad guy. Having a mummy wake up and having his greatest enemy before him would make little thematic sense and make for a really short chronicle. However, waking up and having a much of faceless thugs waiting to get slaughtered would seem like a good way to give the players some chance to use their awesome power before it starts flowing away from them. Having a mummy wake up and do nothing for a week would seem like such a terrible waste since there is a good chance he would lose half of his Sekhem during that time.<br /> <br /> Of course, after this big fight ends, then the clock starts ticking and then the players can do things like socialize, investigate, travel, and do things not related to fighting. However, if they are going to accomplish their mission, they need to do it quickly. Then it becomes a story of a guy dying of some disease and must complete a task as he gets weaker and weaker (which is destined to happen). As they get closer to the main enemy and prepare for the boss fight, they must use their wits as their Sekhem flees away. The end battle is where they must fight a great enemy using their knowledge and wits vs raw power.<br /> <br /> So, if I had to estimate how a default mummy game would be structured, it would be something like this<br /> <br /> Intro: big fight against thugs<br /> <br /> Midgame: Investigation, socialize, learn about their purpose, accumulate memory, some fights against the lieutenants of their enemy. Some uses of awesome power, but their Sekhem is fading, especially if they have been increasing memory.<br /> <br /> End Game: Learn about their purpose and fight their great enemy of the Chronicle, however, their Sekhem has dropped significantly so they must rely on their wits and resources to defeat their foe. The final boss fight is a desperate one as they must economize their remaining Sekhem and no longer have access to high level Utterances. They complete their mission and then fade back into the sleep of ages. <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1107-maryshelly","name":"maryshelly","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1107_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"337"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-10T08:22:19-08:00","id":69092,"title":"","content":"I find that Mummies, IC and OOC, likely feels regret if he can't put all of his Sekhem 10 to use. Sadly, the same is true of the rezz for Golden Ankh, as a Mummy's rising is unlikely to be timed to be within 3-5 minutes of a mortal's death (even if summoned as the mortal is dying). Similarly, if a fight is already going down as a Mummy rises, the situation is fairly dire. I suppose thats more proof that its NOT a one chronicle/one descent game. It gives players a chance to explore the full spectrum of their power, get revitalized by the newly risen power, and to also reimagine the character from its resurrection onwards.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/935-cleverest-of-things","name":"Cleverest of Things","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar935_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"650"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}